  "interpretation": "The individually named OSM point is interior to original building 1617. Separate 2019 and 2025 orthophotos show four small evenly spaced raised dormer roofs on its southern long slope. The preserved city roof outline is a simple rectangle, with roof-edge shifts between orthophotos. The images constrain bay spacing better than eave overhang. They do not constrain an absolute individual storey height or the geometry of the covered northern side. Use the photographic four-bay section as an independent exhibit unless a complete non-overlapping city reconstruction is verified.",
  "uncertainty": "Dormer centre ±2 original pixels (about 0.5 m). Visually corresponding end eaves ±4–5 native px (about 1–1.3 m), with trees on both sides. True +X runs east roughly 86–89 degrees. Do not use the geocoded common gate address as the No. 11 survey point."
